      <sectiondef kind="define">
      <memberdef kind="define" id="column__mask_8h_1abe59cf820dd38e3be4ba5455344d7e5a" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>COLUMN_MASK_FULL</name>
        <initializer>UINT64_MAX</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Column mask is a bitmask of update operations for one tuple. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Column mask bit &apos;n&apos; is set if in the corresponding tuple field &apos;n&apos; could be changed by an update operation. This mask is used for update and upsert optimizations, when, for example, it is necessary to check whether the operation has changed an indexed field.</para><para>The last bit of the mask stands for fields in range [63, +inf). If an update operation updates field #63 and greater, then this last bit of the mask is set. If an update operations changes many fields (&apos;#&apos; or &apos;!&apos;), then all fields after and including the target field could be changed - in such case we set not one bit, but a range of bits. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/home/tsafin/tarantool/src/box/column_mask.h" line="53" column="9" bodyfile="/home/tsafin/tarantool/src/box/column_mask.h" bodystart="53" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      </sectiondef>
